{
  "description": "Cross-platform conformance vectors for a cloud provider health probe's verdict (issue #779). Source of truth: shared-core-rs/crates/hw-net/src/health.rs parse_health_response, which decides `reason` (healthy / unauthorized / unreachable) for every provider; `healthy` is always reason == healthy. 401/403 are unauthorized for every provider; 400 is unauthorized for Gemini, GeminiTranscribe, GeminiTranscribeLive and Grok (they answer an invalid key with 400); ElevenLabs' STT probe sends an empty body, so its 400/422 are healthy; everything else is unreachable. `provider` is the core's HwProvider variant name. Replayed by Rust (shared-core-rs/crates/hw-net/tests/health_vectors.rs), Windows (app/windows/HyperWhisper.SmokeTests, through CloudProviderHealthService.MapHealthVerdict), the portable .NET head (app/shared-dotnet/HyperWhisper.SharedCore.Tests, through the C# binding) and macOS (app/macos/hyperwhisperTests/HealthConformanceVectorTests.swift, through CloudProviderHealthManager.mapRustHealth). Regenerate: cd shared-core-rs && cargo test -p hw-net --test health_vectors -- --ignored regenerate",
